-- A BREACH BY whose party is of the wrong type, as an operand of a RAND under
-- a GIVETH: the error is a type mismatch at the BY expression, as on
-- unstable. Before this branch ported unstable's checkRegulativeBinOp, the
-- first said the party type was not known, and the second pointed at the
-- whole RAND, blaming its second operand. (The adversarial pass of
-- 2026-11-20: BL-5, BL-6.)

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF deliver, noop

-- 1. A list of STRINGs after BY in the second operand.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`a list of the wrong type` MEANS FULFILLED RAND (BREACH BY LIST "x", "y")

-- 2. A STRING after BY in the first operand.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`a party of the wrong type` MEANS
    (BREACH BY "Alice" BECAUSE "late")
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 5)
